Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables and columns for this task  
• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
  – "content": holds the complete file text; has to be split into individual lines so each line can be classified.  
  – "sample_repo_name": lets us restrict‑or group results by repository.  
  – "sample_path": lets us restrict‑or group results by file path / extension (optional).  
  – "id": unique blob id; useful for joining or de‑duplicating.  

Optional supporting table  
• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES  
  – "repo_name", "path", "id": can be joined to SAMPLE_CONTENTS through the blob "id" if path‑level metadata is needed.

Typical conditions / predicates you might use  
• WHERE "sample_repo_name" = '<some_repo>' ‑‑ focus on one repo  
• WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%.c'          ‑‑ focus on C source files  
• RLIKE '\\s+$'        ‑‑ detect “trailing” lines (end with blank char)  
• RLIKE '^ +'          ‑‑ detect “Space” lines (start with a space)  
• NOT ( …trailing OR …Space…)  ‑‑ classify as “Other”

Below are ten incremental Snowflake SQL snippets (each limited to 20 rows) that help explore the data and eventually produce the desired report.  
All column names are enclosed in double quotation marks and the fully‑qualified names use DATABASE.SCHEMA.TABLE format exactly as required.

```sql
-- 1. Preview a handful of content blobs to understand the raw text
SELECT 
  "sample_repo_name",
  "sample_path",
  "content"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Peek at files of a single repository to narrow the scope
SELECT 
  "sample_path",
  "size",
  "content"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_repo_name" = 'dorimanx/DORIMANX_LG_STOCK_LP_KERNEL'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Split the text of one blob into individual lines (using LATERAL FLATTEN)
SELECT 
  c."sample_repo_name",
  c."sample_path",
  f.value::STRING AS "line"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(c."content", '\n')) f
WHERE c."sample_repo_name" = 'dorimanx/DORIMANX_LG_STOCK_LP_KERNEL'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Show lines that END with at least one blank (space or tab) – “trailing”
SELECT 
  f.value::STRING AS "line_with_trailing_space"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(c."content", '\n')) f
WHERE f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Show lines that START with a space – “Space” category
SELECT 
  f.value::STRING AS "line_starting_with_space"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(c."content", '\n')) f
WHERE f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Show lines that are NEITHER “trailing” nor “Space” – “Other”
SELECT 
  f.value::STRING AS "other_line"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(c."content", '\n')) f
WHERE NOT (f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$' OR f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Count the three categories for one specific file
SELECT
  c."sample_repo_name",
  c."sample_path",
  SUM(CASE WHEN f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$'                 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "trailing_cnt",
  SUM(CASE WHEN f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +'                   THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "space_cnt",
  SUM(CASE WHEN NOT (f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$' OR f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "other_cnt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(c."content", '\n')) f
WHERE c."sample_path" = 'drivers/isdn/hisax/elsa.c'
GROUP BY c."sample_repo_name", c."sample_path"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Aggregate the three categories per repository (all its files combined)
SELECT
  c."sample_repo_name",
  SUM(CASE WHEN f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$'                 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "trailing_lines",
  SUM(CASE WHEN f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +'                   THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "space_lines",
  SUM(CASE WHEN NOT (f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$' OR f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "other_lines"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(c."content", '\n')) f
GROUP BY c."sample_repo_name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Grand totals across ALL repositories (no grouping)
SELECT
  SUM(CASE WHEN f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$'                 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "total_trailing",
  SUM(CASE WHEN f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +'                   THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "total_space",
  SUM(CASE WHEN NOT (f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$' OR f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "total_other"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(c."content", '\n')) f
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Same as #9 but also include a sanity check on total number of lines
SELECT
  COUNT(*)                                                  AS "total_lines",
  SUM(IFF(f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$', 1, 0))             AS "trailing",
  SUM(IFF(f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +', 1, 0))               AS "space",
  SUM(IFF(NOT (f.value::STRING RLIKE '\\s+$' OR f.value::STRING RLIKE '^ +'), 1, 0)) AS "other"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => SPLIT(c."content", '\n')) f
LIMIT 20;
```

